{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "40-new-features-20-project-state-and-events-30-run",
  "title": "Run State",
  "root": "b-run-root",
  "blocks": {
    "b-run-root": {
      "id": "b-run-root",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "concepts": [
          "run",
          "scheduler",
          "epochs",
          "recovery",
          "remote-application"
        ]
      },
      "children": [
        "b-project-state-run-p",
        "b-project-state-run-decision-sync-survival",
        "b-project-state-run-sync-survival-heading",
        "b-project-state-run-sync-survival-mechanics",
        "b-project-state-run-sync-rebase-li",
        "b-project-state-run-sync-conflicts-li",
        "b-project-state-run-sync-boundary-li",
        "b-project-state-run-sync-survival-invariants",
        "b-project-state-run-fixed-baseline-li",
        "b-project-state-run-moving-head-li",
        "b-project-state-run-boundary-ownership-li",
        "b-project-state-run-shape",
        "b-project-state-run-statuses",
        "b-project-state-run-decision-recovery",
        "b-project-state-run-recovery-heading",
        "b-project-state-run-recovery-mechanics",
        "b-project-state-run-recovery-system-transition-li",
        "b-project-state-run-recovery-operator-transition-li",
        "b-project-state-run-recovery-rationale",
        "b-project-state-run-recovery-identity-li",
        "b-project-state-run-recovery-history-li",
        "b-project-state-run-recovery-prominence-li",
        "b-project-state-scheduler-conditions"
      ]
    },
    "b-project-state-run-p": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-p",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A run is one autonomous scheduling effort against an immutable original baseline and policy revision. Pause, resume, and upstream sync all retain the run identity: sync rebases the session worktree onto new upstream work and records the application as a remote-application boundary in the run's own timeline. Background knowledge may advance while the run is active, so scheduler decisions and worker packets record the knowledge revision they actually consume."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-decision-sync-survival": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-decision-sync-survival",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "kind": "decision",
        "title": "Decision (2026-08-11) — runs survive sync via remote-application boundaries",
        "tone": "success"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Sync does not close the interrupted run. Upstream changes enter the timeline as remote-application boundaries while the run identity and original baseline stay fixed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-sync-survival-heading": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-sync-survival-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "How a Run Survives Sync"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-sync-survival-mechanics": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-sync-survival-mechanics",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "When sync advances the upstream revision:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-sync-rebase-li": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-sync-rebase-li",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "It first rebases the session worktree onto the new upstream work."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-sync-conflicts-li": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-sync-conflicts-li",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "That rebase passes through the run's completed epoch history and resolves merge conflicts against the session head."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-sync-boundary-li": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-sync-boundary-li",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The resulting application enters the run's timeline as a remote-application boundary: an epoch-completion-like record on top of the last completed epoch, with its own score delta for whatever upstream contributed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-sync-survival-invariants": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-sync-survival-invariants",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Run continuity separates the fixed origin of the effort from the head it currently plans against:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-fixed-baseline-li": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-fixed-baseline-li",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The run identity and base_revision remain unchanged as the original baseline, so nothing is rebuilt from scratch; the session continues, and the scheduler recomputes its next candidates against the new head_revision."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-moving-head-li": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-moving-head-li",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "head_revision is the moving value, and only remote-application boundaries advance it."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-boundary-ownership-li": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-boundary-ownership-li",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Per the session-container decision, the boundary record belongs to the session timeline: an active run references it, while a sync with no active run attaches it to the session alone."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-shape": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-shape",
      "type": "state-shape",
      "props": {
        "description": "Run control, scheduling position, progress, queue summaries, references, and tracing.",
        "example": "{\n  \"run_id\": \"run-2026-08-11-01\",\n  \"project_id\": \"melee\",\n  \"session_id\": \"session-7\",\n  \"revision\": 288,\n  \"inputs\": {\n    \"base_revision\": \"upstream-9ac4\",\n    \"policy_revision\": \"policy-42\",\n    \"starting_knowledge_revision\": \"knowledge-375\",\n    \"configuration_snapshot\": {\n      \"desired_workers\": 64,\n      \"epoch_size\": 64\n    }\n  },\n  \"head_revision\": \"upstream-9ba1\",\n  \"control\": {\n    \"status\": \"draining\",\n    \"stop_request\": {\n      \"target\": \"sync\",\n      \"mode\": \"finish_epoch\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"scheduling\": {\n    \"active_epoch_id\": \"epoch-19\",\n    \"desired_workers\": 64,\n    \"scheduler_condition\": \"boundary\",\n    \"admitted\": 64,\n    \"claimed\": 64,\n    \"running\": 2\n  },\n  \"progress\": {\n    \"baseline_score\": 72.642,\n    \"confirmed_score\": 73.147,\n    \"tentative_changes\": 2,\n    \"confirmed_changes\": 31,\n    \"regressed_changes\": 1\n  },\n  \"integration_queue\": {\n    \"pending\": 1,\n    \"conflicts\": 0\n  },\n  \"epoch_ids\": [\n    \"epoch-18\",\n    \"epoch-19\"\n  ],\n  \"remote_application_ids\": [\n    \"remote-application-3\"\n  ],\n  \"worker_state_ids\": [\n    \"worker-state-501\",\n    \"worker-state-502\"\n  ],\n  \"checkpoint_ids\": [\n    \"checkpoint-88\"\n  ],\n  \"active_operation_ids\": [\n    \"operation-run-drain-44\"\n  ],\n  \"latest_event_sequence\": 92811,\n  \"blockers\": []\n}",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "run_id",
            "type": "RunId"
          },
          {
            "name": "project_id",
            "type": "ProjectId"
          },
          {
            "name": "session_id",
            "type": "SessionId",
            "description": "Owning session container."
          },
          {
            "name": "revision",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          {
            "name": "inputs",
            "type": "RunInputs",
            "fields": [
              {
                "name": "base_revision",
                "type": "SourceRevision",
                "description": "Original baseline. Immutable — upstream arrives as remote-application boundaries, never by rewriting this."
              },
              {
                "name": "policy_revision",
                "type": "PolicyRevision",
                "description": "Immutable after activation."
              },
              {
                "name": "starting_knowledge_revision",
                "type": "KnowledgeRevision"
              },
              {
                "name": "configuration_snapshot",
                "type": "RunConfiguration"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "head_revision",
            "type": "SourceRevision",
            "description": "Mirror of the owning session's head, which the scheduler plans against. The session owns head lineage; equals base_revision until a remote-application boundary advances it."
          },
          {
            "name": "control",
            "type": "RunControl",
            "fields": [
              {
                "name": "status",
                "type": "\"draft\" | \"ready\" | \"active\" | \"draining\" | \"paused\" | \"completed\" | \"failed\" | \"cancelled\""
              },
              {
                "name": "stop_request",
                "type": "StopRequest",
                "required": false
              },
              {
                "name": "terminal_reason",
                "type": "string",
                "required": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "scheduling",
            "type": "RunScheduling",
            "fields": [
              {
                "name": "active_epoch_id",
                "type": "EpochId | null"
              },
              {
                "name": "desired_workers",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "name": "scheduler_condition",
                "type": "\"idle\" | \"planning\" | \"dispatching\" | \"waiting\" | \"boundary\" | \"blocked\""
              },
              {
                "name": "admitted",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "name": "claimed",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "name": "running",
                "type": "integer"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "progress",
            "type": "RunProgress",
            "fields": [
              {
                "name": "baseline_score",
                "type": "number"
              },
              {
                "name": "confirmed_score",
                "type": "number"
              },
              {
                "name": "tentative_changes",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "name": "confirmed_changes",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "name": "regressed_changes",
                "type": "integer"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "integration_queue",
            "type": "IntegrationQueueSummary"
          },
          {
            "name": "epoch_ids",
            "type": "EpochId[]"
          },
          {
            "name": "remote_application_ids",
            "type": "RemoteApplicationId[]",
            "description": "Remote-application boundaries in timeline order, each recording prior head, applied upstream revision, resolved conflicts, and score delta."
          },
          {
            "name": "worker_state_ids",
            "type": "WorkerStateId[]"
          },
          {
            "name": "checkpoint_ids",
            "type": "CheckpointId[]"
          },
          {
            "name": "active_operation_ids",
            "type": "OperationId[]"
          },
          {
            "name": "latest_event_sequence",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          {
            "name": "blockers",
            "type": "Blocker[]"
          }
        ],
        "name": "RunState"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-statuses": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-statuses",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Status",
          "Meaning",
          "Stable invariant"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "draft",
            "Inputs or configuration are incomplete.",
            "No scheduler or worker may start."
          ],
          [
            "ready",
            "Required inputs are captured and readiness gates pass.",
            "Activation cannot change the bound base or policy revisions."
          ],
          [
            "active",
            "Autonomous scheduling authority is enabled.",
            "The run holds the project dispatch lease."
          ],
          [
            "draining",
            "New admission is disabled while existing work settles.",
            "No new claims are created."
          ],
          [
            "paused",
            "Scheduling is disabled and the run remains resumable.",
            "Existing work has settled or been explicitly recovered."
          ],
          [
            "completed",
            "Autonomous work closed normally.",
            "The run cannot resume or admit work."
          ],
          [
            "failed",
            "The runner could not safely continue.",
            "Recovery returns the run to paused on the same identity; only completed and cancelled are terminal."
          ],
          [
            "cancelled",
            "The operator abandoned the run.",
            "Evidence remains readable; the run cannot resume."
          ]
        ],
        "title": "Run status values"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-decision-recovery": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-decision-recovery",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "kind": "decision",
        "title": "Decision (2026-08-11) — failed runs resume in place",
        "tone": "success"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Recovery never creates a successor run. Failed runs return to paused on the same run identity, and only completed and cancelled are terminal."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-recovery-heading": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-recovery-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "How In-Place Recovery Works"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-recovery-mechanics": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-recovery-mechanics",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Recovery resumes a failed run in place through separate system and operator transitions:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-recovery-system-transition-li": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-recovery-system-transition-li",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The recovery operation settles or cancels orphaned claims and operations, emits run.recovered naming every cancelled subject, and moves the run failed → paused."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-recovery-operator-transition-li": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-recovery-operator-transition-li",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The operator then resumes it paused → active as usual; only completed and cancelled are terminal statuses."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-recovery-rationale": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-recovery-rationale",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Resuming in place extends the continuity chosen for sync survival and session lineage:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-recovery-identity-li": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-recovery-identity-li",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The run id persists across every interruption rather than giving recovery a successor identity."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-recovery-history-li": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-recovery-history-li",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The cost of that continuity is retained recovery history, including cancelled claims and partial epochs."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-run-recovery-prominence-li": {
      "id": "b-project-state-run-recovery-prominence-li",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The trace and UI must therefore make the recovery point prominent so it does not blend into normal history."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-project-state-scheduler-conditions": {
      "id": "b-project-state-scheduler-conditions",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Condition",
          "Meaning"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "idle",
            "No scheduler operation is executing."
          ],
          [
            "planning",
            "Candidate evidence is being reduced into an admission decision."
          ],
          [
            "dispatching",
            "Admitted work is being assigned to available capacity."
          ],
          [
            "waiting",
            "The active run is sleeping until a durable wake event arrives."
          ],
          [
            "boundary",
            "Confirmation, integration, report refresh, or save-point work is executing."
          ],
          [
            "blocked",
            "The active run cannot progress without recovery or operator action."
          ]
        ],
        "title": "Scheduler condition values"
      },
      "children": []
    }
  }
}
